<title>UK: Unilever gains, added to NatWest 15 list.</title>
<headline>Unilever gains, added to NatWest 15 list.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Unilever Plc rose to a seven-month high on Thursday as the anglo-Dutch consumer products group was added to NatWest Securities' top 15 list of selected stocks, market sources said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 14p at 13.22 stg by 1105 GMT, after earlier rising as high as 13.28 stg, its highest since February. NatWest strategists were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Vodafone Group Plc was dropped from the list, after the mobile 'phone group was yesterday cut to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;add&quot; by NatWest analysts.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
